Z||000024||fogglethorpe||10-18-2001||08:53 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by frontal lobe:<BR><B>It's time for the U.S. to retire the penny.  It actually costs a lot to keep it in circulation.<P>Also, the treasury wants to get rid of the paper dollar and go to coins as it would save millions of dollars, but the populace has been resistant.  No wonder, considering the doofuses (is that the correct plural of doofus?) first gave us Susan B. Anthony, and then on their second attempt gave us a dollar almost indistinguishable from a quarter.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Paper money (actually a Federal Reserve "Note") is technically worthless. Sure, you can buy goods and services with it, but in the event of an economic collapse, you might as well line the bird cage with it. There is no gold to back it up...it is essentially an IOU.<BR>Our coins are the same...they are alloys, not gold or silver as they once were. The reason for this is something called "The Federal Reserve Act", signed by President Wilson just after WW1. This unconstitutional act took the power to mint money and regulate its value away from the Federal Government, and gave it to a non-elected, private entity. It basically bastardized our money supply.<P>....................<BR>(No charge for the history lesson)<P>||||reg||1
